# overlay/base/packages.list — the DPorts packages every profile gets.
#
# Copyright (c) 2026 The wtfbsd contributors. BSD-2-Clause (see LICENSE).
#
# One DPorts ORIGIN per line (category/port); blank lines and
# #-comments are ignored. The build hands the packages to the release
# tooling of DragonFly, which puts them into the release root:
#
#   DPORTS_EXTRA_PACKAGES="<the packages of the base list and of the
#                            profile list>"
#
# The names are DPorts origins and not bare package names: dsynth takes
# origins only (category/port), and a bare name is only understood under
# the binpkgs modifier of the release tooling, which this template does
# not use. The release tooling builds them from the DPorts tree, whose
# path is DPORTS_PATH (/usr/dports by default).
#
# They are plain data, so a site can correct them in this file without
# touching the build. The names are not verified by this template (see
# the round report).
#
# security/ca_root_nss: the name service switch of the base system, so
# that the accounts of the first boot are found.
# security/doas: the privilege escalation of the product; the overlay
# ships /usr/local/etc/doas.conf with "permit persist :wheel".
#
security/ca_root_nss
security/doas
